## Leaf rules

- Never revert a change you did not make; no `git commit`, `stash`, `checkout`, `reset` or `restore`.
- Never a foreground `sleep`: `run_in_background` and wait for the notification, a background `until` loop, or
  `claude-code agents result -f <id>`; no `sudo` or `git switch`; read history with `git show <rev>:<path>` or `git log`.
- Write file content that names a blocked command with the Write or Edit tool, never a shell heredoc.
- Edit source with Edit or Write, never a splice script, `sed -i` or `perl -pi`; mutation-test a copy under `$TMPDIR`;
  no `rm -rf` outside `$TMPDIR` or scratch dirs; never print a credential variable, even piped to `grep`.
- Edit only the owned files; a package owns the `_test.go` of each owned source file. A compile error in a file you do
  not own is reported, not fixed.
- Tests, by default: basic tests that a new feature works (a couple of seconds at most); a bug fix shows its live
  before/after run; other cases are proposals in the hand-back (case, what it guards, runtime); need more, say why.
- Shell output you read goes through rtk: `rtk git|go|grep|rg|ls|find|diff|wc …`, `rtk grep -n`, `rtk git diff`, `rtk go test`; one file
  is the Read tool, never cat/head; exact bytes: `rtk bypass <cmd>`.
- Order: format → lint → live check → your package or exact tests (`go test -run '^TestX$' <pkg>`) → Skill(simplify); never `./...`.
- A relay waiting on this job: the moment `claude-code agents result -f <id>` returns with the job ended, hand back
  the job's result as your next action; do nothing in between.
- Code leaves run on the Databricks arm (`/coworker`'s default overlay `{"provider":"databricks","profile":"auto",
  "remote":"auto"}`), spread over dev/qa/prod; docs leaves on claude sonnet.

